   2323  f760							; ==============================================================================
   2324  f760							; Phase 5 — second GRP1 object (no flicker). TIA has one GRP1 sprite, so two
   2325  f760							; objects in a room used to alternate frames (30 Hz flicker each). When they
   2326  f760							; live in DIFFERENT cave bands each can be drawn on ALL of its scanlines: the
   2327  f760							; band's setup swaps the live trio (ObjBase/ObjTop/ActiveObjectX) for slot 1
   2328  f760							; and repositions P1 there. The per-line object path is untouched — it already
   2329  f760							; draws from the live trio and takes COLUP1 from ObjColorTab[ObjBase+row].
   2330  f760							;
   2331  f760							; Invariant (do not relax): slot 1's band is STRICTLY HIGHER than slot 0's.
   2332  f760							; Bands are set up 0->1->2, so no later band has to restore slot 0's trio.
   2333  f760							; Rooms whose two objects share a band keep the old behaviour (slot 0 only,
   2334  f760							; rotation in SelectActiveObject unchanged).
   2335  f760							; Cost: the band-compare early-out sits in the setup line's free tail (0
   2336  f760							; lines); a band that DOES host slot 1 pays 2 lines (SetObjectXPos must start
   2337  f760							; on a line boundary and the HMOVE needs the next line's HBLANK).
   2338  f760							;
   2339  f760							; StageSlot1 (VBLANK, after SelectActiveObject): stages ObjBase1/ObjTop1/ObjX1,
   2340  f760							; $FF = none. Slot 1 = the miner or the first live enemy whose Y is in a band
   2341  f760							; above slot 0's. The KEY skip mirrors the slot-0 path (KeyHeld = LevelStartRoom
   2342  f760							; b7). Tally frames ($FE) are gated out: EnemyRamY holds score-pointer bytes
   2343  f760							; then (AGENTS: tally frame draws the MINER only).
