   3865  fe90							; FoldIndirect — cross-bank data fetch (HERO fold, write-triggered;
   3866  fe90							; level_bank_plan §0.1). Pad lands $FEF6-$FEFF (last byte ≤ $FEFF — $FF00
   3867  fe90							; stays the fineAdjust anchor). Bytes must be byte-identical in bank2
   3868  fe90							; (guard: verify_build) — after `sta $1FF8` the CPU fetches the remainder
   3869  fe90							; from the data bank at the same PC.
   3870  fe90							; Contract: bank select is ABSOLUTE $1FF8 (bank2) — X/Y both preserved,
   3871  fe90							; A = junk in, data out (`sta $1FF6` switches back, A preserved).
   3872  fe90							; P3.1 deviation (plan §0): `sta $1FF8,X` required X=0, but every enemy
   3873  fe90							; loop keeps the slot in X and has no free temp to swap (DEY/snake hold
   3874  fe90							; Temp live across the read). All level data is bank2, so X-selection is
   3875  fe90							; dead weight; bank3 data later needs a second entry `sta $1FF9` pad.
   3876  fe90							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
